    {
      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.3,
      "end": 2.48,
      "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.04,
      "end": 17.27,
      "text": "Doable. The trick on a tight budget is putting most of the money into the graphics card, since that matters most for games."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 19.46,
      "end": 27.75,
      "text": "A mid range processor is plenty. Sixteen gigabytes of memory, and a solid state drive so games load fast. Don't overspend on a fancy case."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.77,
      "end": 34.57,
      "text": "I'm fairly sure about it, but I could be wrong. What sounds off to you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 38.78,
      "end": 46.32,
      "text": "Used graphics cards can be great value, just buy from someone with good feedback and test it if you can. I'd buy the power supply new though."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 50.17,
      "end": 55.71,
      "text": "A cheap or worn out one can fail and take other parts with it. It's not exciting, but it protects everything else."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 63.26,
      "end": 68.31,
      "text": "Most people are the first time. Follow a video slowly, and it's really just careful Lego."
    }
  ]
